   "text": "Reading the drawing region by region:\n\n- **Macrocycle backbone:** the ring runs Orn \u2192 Lys \u2192 N-Me-Trp, then an aryl-CH2-NH link, and finally back to the Orn \u03b1-NH through a pyridyl-CH2.\n- **Ornithine:** the side chain is H2N-CH2CH2CH2- on the \u03b1-carbon. The \u03b1-NH is bonded to a CH2 on the pyridine, and the \u03b1-carbonyl links to the lysine NH.\n- **Lysine:** the side chain is 4 carbons ending in NH2. Its carbonyl is bonded to N(CH3) of the tryptophan.\n- **Tryptophan:** the \u03b1-carbon carries CH2 attached to indol-3-yl. Its carbonyl is bonded to NH-CH2 on the benzene ring.\n- **Aryl linkage:** the pyridine C3 bears the CH2NH and C2 bears the S. The S connects to a benzene carbon that has an ortho CH3 on one side and an ortho CH2NH on the other. The benzene carbon next to the CH2NH carbon carries a 2-oxo-pyridin-4-yl group whose ring N bears CH2COOH.\n- **Stereochemistry:** all three wedged \u03b1-carbons work out to S (the L-amino-acid configuration) when I assign CIP priorities from the wedge geometry. I wrote each in its L-amino-acid SMILES pattern and checked the neighbour order for each tag.\n\nSMILES: NCCC[C@H]1C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCCN)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](Cc2c[nH]c3ccccc23)C(=O)NCc2c(-c3ccn(CC(=O)O)c(=O)c3)ccc(C)c2Sc2ncccc2CN1"
